  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "DictionaryMemo::AddDictionaryDelta",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/ipc/dictionary.cc",
    "description": "`AddDictionaryDelta()` constructs arrays from untrusted `ArrayData` using `MakeArray(original_dict)` and `MakeArray(dictionary)` *before* validating them. For malformed IPC dictionary-delta payloads, `MakeArray()` instantiates nested `ListArray`/`DictionaryArray` objects whose constructors contain `ARROW_CHECK` invariants (e.g., non-null dictionary pointer in `DictionaryArray`), causing a fatal log and `abort()` instead of returning a recoverable `Status`. The crash surfaces in logging (`CerrLog::~CerrLog`) but the root cause is missing pre-validation / unsafe object construction in `AddDictionaryDelta`.",
    "conditions": "In `arrow-ipc-stream-fuzz`, attacker-controlled IPC stream data is parsed in `ReadDictionary()` (`reader.cc`) and passed as `dict_data` into `DictionaryMemo::AddDictionaryDelta()` when `isDelta` is set. If the stream defines a dictionary delta whose nested array metadata is inconsistent (notably dictionary-typed child data with `data->dictionary == nullptr`), `AddDictionaryDelta()` calls `MakeArray()` on that malformed data, triggering `ARROW_CHECK` abort during array construction. Trigger requires a dictionary-delta message with malformed nested dictionary/list structure reaching `AddDictionaryDelta` prior to successful validation."
  },
